      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{3{n}^{2}+15n+18}{{n}^{2}+4n+4}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We factor the numerator and denominator, canceling out any common factors that appear in both.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{n}^{2}+15n+18}{{n}^{2}+4n+4} & =\\frac{3({n}^{2}+5n+6)}{{n}^{2}+4n+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(n+3)(n+2)}{(n+2)(n+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(n+3)\\cancel{(n+2)}}{(n+2)\\cancel{(n+2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(n+3)}{n+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3n+9}{n+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
